    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\nProgressive delivery and [Vault](https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/docs)-style secrets for AI platforms.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[Canary vs blue-green vs roll]\n  N0 --> N1[Feature flags for AI]\n  N1 --> N2[Secrets and KMS]\n  N2 --> N3[GitOps/ArgoCD role]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((MLOps Q A Canary blue-green feature flag))\n    Canary Deployments\n    Blue-Green Deployments\n    Rolling Updates\n    Feature Flags\n    GitOps Workflows\n    Infrastructure-as-Code\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. Canary vs blue-green vs rolling?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nCanary: tiny % traffic to new model/prompt. Blue-green: two full environments, instant switch. Rolling: gradually replace pods. Prefer canary for LLM quality risk.\n\n### Q2. Feature flags for AI?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nToggle prompts, tools, models, and RAG corpora per cohort. Combine with kill switches when cost or toxicity spikes.\n\n### Q3. Secrets and KMS?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nStore API keys in Vault/cloud KMS — never in git or images. Short-lived creds, rotation, and audit access to model providers.\n\n### Q4. GitOps/ArgoCD role?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nDeclarative desired state for k8s services; CI builds images, CD reconciles cluster. Keep model artifacts referenced by digest.\n\n## Official references\n- [Vault docs](https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/docs) · [Kubernetes](https://kubernetes.io/docs/home/)\n",
