    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\nClassical testing disciplines applied to LLM/tooling codebases.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[What is unit-testable in Gen]\n  N0 --> N1[TDD vs BDD]\n  N1 --> N2[Load/stress/security testing]\n  N2 --> N3[Regression for prompts]\n  N3 --> N4[Key takeaway]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Engineering Q A TDD BDD and the testing ))\n    Test-Driven Development\n    TDD\n    Behavior-Driven Developm\n    BDD\n    Unit Testing\n    Integration Testing\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. What is unit-testable in GenAI apps?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nParsers, routers, schema validators, ranking functions, chunkers, and policy engines. Keep pure logic out of prompt strings when possible.\n\n### Q2. TDD vs BDD?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nTDD drives design via failing tests. BDD specifies behavior in domain language (Given/When/Then) — great for product acceptance of AI features.\n\n### Q3. Load/stress/security testing?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nLoad: sustainable QPS/latency. Stress: breaking points. Security: injection, authz bypass, secret leakage in logs/traces.\n\n### Q4. Regression for prompts?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nGolden sets + thresholds in CI. Fail the build when faithfulness/toxicity/cost regresses past budget.\n\n## Key takeaway\nAI products still need a testing pyramid — evals sit on top of solid unit/integration layers.\n",
