    "excerpt": "Edge and mesh patterns in front of model services (~3-min).",
    "sourceUrl": "https://learnhub.local/genai/qa-istio-gateway-cache-cdn",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-23T17:30:28.350Z",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\n[Istio](https://istio.io/latest/docs/) and edge patterns for scalable AI APIs.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[What does a service mesh buy]\n  N0 --> N1[API gateway vs reverse proxy]\n  N1 --> N2[Caching strategies for GenAI]\n  N2 --> N3[CDN role]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Cloud Q A Service mesh API gateway cachi))\n    Istio\n    Service Mesh\n    API Gateway\n    Reverse Proxy\n    Caching Strategies\n    CDN Integration\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. What does a service mesh buy you?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nmTLS, retries, traffic splitting, and observability between microservices without app rewrites — useful when many model/tool services talk privately.\n\n### Q2. API gateway vs reverse proxy?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nGateway: auth, rate limits, routing, WAF at the edge. Reverse proxy: TLS termination and load balancing. Often combined (CDN → gateway → mesh).\n\n### Q3. Caching strategies for GenAI?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nCache embeddings, retrieval results, and idempotent tool responses. Be careful caching model completions (personalization, privacy, staleness).\n\n### Q4. CDN role?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nStatic assets, model cards, and sometimes edge workers — not a substitute for GPU inference unless using edge-capable runtimes.\n\n## Official references\n- [Istio docs](https://istio.io/latest/docs/)\n",
