    "content": "## Scope\n[OpenTelemetry](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/), [Prometheus](https://prometheus.io/docs/), [Grafana](https://grafana.com/docs/).\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[Golden signals for LLM servi]\n  N0 --> N1[Why OpenTelemetry]\n  N1 --> N2[Prometheus + Grafana role]\n  N2 --> N3[Logs platforms ELK/Splunk]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Cloud Q A Observability Prometheus Grafa))\n    Observability\n    Prometheus\n    Grafana\n    OpenTelemetry\n    Jaeger\n    Zipkin\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. Golden signals for LLM services?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nLatency, traffic, errors, saturation — plus token cost, cache hit rate, retrieval empty rate, and guardrail blocks.\n\n### Q2. Why OpenTelemetry?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nVendor-neutral instrumentation for traces/metrics/logs. Export to Jaeger/Zipkin, Datadog, New Relic, or Grafana stacks without rewriting apps.\n\n### Q3. Prometheus + Grafana role?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nProm scrapes metrics; Grafana dashboards/alerts. Ideal for k8s-native AI platforms.\n\n### Q4. Logs platforms (ELK/Splunk)?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nLong-term search and audit. Redact prompts/PII. Correlate log fields with trace IDs.\n\n## Official references\n- [OpenTelemetry](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/) · [Prometheus](https://prometheus.io/docs/) · [Grafana](https://grafana.com/docs/)\n",
