    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\n[Ragas](https://docs.ragas.io/), structured generation patterns, and [OpenAI APIs](https://platform.openai.com/docs/) eval workflows.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[What is Ragas for]\n  N0 --> N1[Outlines / constrained decod]\n  N1 --> N2[Rebuff and prompt-injection ]\n  N2 --> N3[OpenAI platform evals]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Tools Q A Ragas Outlines Rebuff and Open))\n    Ragas\n    Outlines\n    Rebuff\n    OpenAI APIs\n    Prompt Evaluation\n    AI Evaluation\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. What is Ragas for?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nRAG evaluation metrics (faithfulness, answer relevancy, context precision/recall) so retrieval changes are measurable — not vibes-based.\n\n### Q2. Outlines / constrained decoding?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nForce outputs to schemas/grammars (JSON, regex) to reduce parse failures in tool-calling and extraction pipelines.\n\n### Q3. Rebuff and prompt-injection defense?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nDetect/block malicious prompts before they reach tools or sensitive resources. Pair with allowlisted tools and output filters.\n\n### Q4. OpenAI platform evals?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nUse provider eval tooling plus your own golden sets. Never rely on a single judge model without human spot checks.\n\n## Official references\n- [Ragas](https://docs.ragas.io/) · [OpenAI docs](https://platform.openai.com/docs/)\n",
