    "excerpt": "Make AI features testable — goldens, determinism, and debug loops (~3-min).",
    "sourceUrl": "https://learnhub.local/genai/qa-deterministic-verification",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-23T17:30:28.214Z",
    "level": "Advanced",
    "content": "## Scope\nEngineering practices that keep non-deterministic models shippable.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[What is a golden reference s]\n  N0 --> N1[How do you get determinism w]\n  N1 --> N2[AI debugging workflow]\n  N2 --> N3[Optimization without breakin]\n  N3 --> N4[Key takeaway]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((AI Q A Deterministic verification golden))\n    Deterministic Verificati\n    Golden Reference Solutio\n    AI Debugging\n    AI Evaluation\n    AI Optimization\n    Prompt Evaluation\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. What is a golden reference solution?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nA trusted expected output (or rubric) for a fixed input — used in regression suites. For LLMs, goldens may be exact strings, JSON schemas, or graded criteria (faithfulness, toxicity).\n\n### Q2. How do you get determinism where possible?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nPin model versions, seeds where supported, temperature=0 for checks, freeze prompts/tools, snapshot retrieval corpora, and stub tools in unit tests.\n\n### Q3. AI debugging workflow?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nReproduce → isolate (prompt vs retrieval vs tool vs model) → compare traces → add failing golden → fix → re-run eval suite. Prefer Langfuse/OTel traces over guesswork.\n\n### Q4. Optimization without breaking quality?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nChange one variable; track cost/latency/quality. Canary new prompts/models; never optimize solely for speed if groundedness drops.\n\n## Key takeaway\nTreat evals and goldens as the compiler for AI systems.\n",
