    "content": "## Scope\n[OpenCV](https://docs.opencv.org/), [spaCy](https://spacy.io/usage), and modern ASR/TTS around LLM products.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[Where does classic CV still ]\n  N0 --> N1[Classification vs detection]\n  N1 --> N2[Speech recognition and TTS i]\n  N2 --> N3[spaCy/NLTK vs LLMs for NLP]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((AI Q A Computer vision speech and multim))\n    Computer Vision\n    Image Classification\n    Object Detection\n    OpenCV\n    Speech Recognition\n    Text-to-Speech\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. Where does classic CV still matter?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nPreprocessing, geometric transforms, classical detectors, and on-device pipelines. OpenCV remains the Swiss Army knife before deep models.\n\n### Q2. Classification vs detection?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nClassification: one label per image. Detection: boxes/masks + classes (YOLO/DETR families). Choose by product need — “is there X?” vs “where are all Xs?”\n\n### Q3. Speech recognition and TTS in GenAI apps?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nASR → text for LLM; TTS for voice UX. Watch latency, diarization, and PII in audio. Prefer streaming ASR for agents.\n\n### Q4. spaCy/NLTK vs LLMs for NLP?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nspaCy/NLTK: fast deterministic pipelines (tokenize, NER) with low cost. LLMs: flexible understanding/generation. Hybrid: rules/entities for structure, LLM for reasoning.\n\n## Official references\n- [OpenCV](https://docs.opencv.org/) · [spaCy](https://spacy.io/usage)\n",
