    "excerpt": "How modern generative families differ — training signal, sampling, failure modes (~3-min).",
    "sourceUrl": "https://learnhub.local/genai/qa-gans-vae-diffusion",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-23T17:30:28.177Z",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\nGenerative modeling families used beyond LLMs (images, audio, latent compression).\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[GANs in one sentence]\n  N0 --> N1[What are VAEs good for]\n  N1 --> N2[Why diffusion models dominat]\n  N2 --> N3[How does this relate to LLMs]\n  N3 --> N4[Key takeaway]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((AI Q A Generative models GANs VAEs and d))\n    Generative Models\n    GANs\n    Variational Autoencoders\n    Diffusion Models\n    Deep Learning\n    Neural Networks\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. GANs in one sentence?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nGenerator vs discriminator adversarial training — sharp samples historically, but training instability and mode collapse are classic failure modes.\n\n### Q2. What are VAEs good for?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nEncoder/decoder with latent probabilistic bottleneck — strong for representation learning, compression, and controllable latents; samples often blurrier than GANs/diffusion.\n\n### Q3. Why diffusion models dominate image gen?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nIterative denoising from noise → data yields high fidelity and controllable conditioning (text, image). Cost: many sampling steps unless distilled/accelerated.\n\n### Q4. How does this relate to LLMs?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nDifferent modality stacks, but shared themes: latents, conditioning, guidance, eval metrics, and serving latency. Multimodal systems often combine diffusion (pixels) + transformers (language).\n\n## Key takeaway\nPick the generative family by modality, controllability needs, and serving budget — not hype.\n",
