    "excerpt": "RL fundamentals for AI engineers — MDPs, algorithms, and env design (~3-min).",
    "sourceUrl": "https://learnhub.local/genai/qa-reinforcement-learning-deep",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-23T17:30:28.161Z",
    "level": "Advanced",
    "content": "## Scope\nRL mental model aligned with [Gymnasium](https://gymnasium.farama.org/)-style environments and standard algorithms.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[What is the RL loop]\n  N0 --> N1[Q-learning vs policy gradien]\n  N1 --> N2[Monte Carlo methods]\n  N2 --> N3[Reward design pitfalls]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((AI Q A Reinforcement learning agents rew))\n    Reinforcement Learning\n    RL Environments\n    Reinforcement Learning A\n    Reward Functions\n    Policy Gradient\n    Q-Learning\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. What is the RL loop?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nAgent observes state, takes action, environment returns reward + next state. Goal: maximize expected return. Formalized as MDP (states, actions, transition, reward, discount).\n\n### Q2. Q-learning vs policy gradient vs actor-critic?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nQ-learning: learn action-values, derive policy (classic off-policy TD). Policy gradient: optimize policy parameters directly from returns. Actor-critic: policy (actor) + value baseline (critic) for lower variance — backbone of many modern deep RL methods.\n\n### Q3. Monte Carlo methods?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nEstimate returns from complete episodes (no bootstrapping). Simple and unbiased but high variance / needs episode termination — contrast with TD methods.\n\n### Q4. Reward design pitfalls?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nSparse rewards, reward hacking, unsafe exploration. Prefer shaped rewards carefully, constrain actions, and evaluate with held-out tasks — not just training return.\n\n## Official references\n- [Gymnasium](https://gymnasium.farama.org/)\n",
