    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\n[Git](https://git-scm.com/doc) workflows and sustainable delivery for large AI repositories.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[What Git practices matter on]\n  N0 --> N1[How should AI PRs be reviewe]\n  N1 --> N2[IDE choices]\n  N2 --> N3[CI/CD for model-related code]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Programming Q A Git code reviews IDEs an))\n    Version Control\n    Git\n    GitHub\n    GitLab\n    Bitbucket\n    Code Reviews\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. What Git practices matter on large AI monorepos?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nSmall PRs, meaningful commits, protected main, signed tags for releases, LFS for large artifacts (sparingly — prefer object storage + checksums for models).\n\n### Q2. How should AI PRs be reviewed?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nCheck eval deltas, prompt/tool contracts, cost/latency impact, secret hygiene, and reproducibility — not only style. Require tests for parsers, routers, and guardrails.\n\n### Q3. IDE choices?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nVS Code + Python/TS for agents; PyCharm/IntelliJ for heavy refactors; remote SSH/devcontainers for GPU boxes. Standardize formatters (ruff/black, prettier) in CI.\n\n### Q4. CI/CD for model-related code?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nLint/test on every PR; build images; run smoke evals; gate deploys on metrics. Separate “code CI” from “model promotion” pipelines.\n\n## Official references\n- [Git documentation](https://git-scm.com/doc)\n",
