    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\n[HTTP semantics](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110), [GraphQL](https://graphql.org/learn/), and architecture patterns for GenAI services.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[REST vs GraphQL for AI produ]\n  N0 --> N1[Useful design patterns in LL]\n  N1 --> N2[OOP vs functional style]\n  N2 --> N3[Secure coding basics for AI ]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Programming Q A APIs microservices Graph))\n    API Development\n    Microservices\n    REST APIs\n    GraphQL\n    Software Architecture\n    Design Patterns\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. REST vs GraphQL for AI products?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nREST/JSON: simple model/predict/chat endpoints, easy caching and gateways. GraphQL: flexible client-shaped reads over metadata/catalogs. Prefer REST for inference SLOs; GraphQL for portal/query layers.\n\n### Q2. Useful design patterns in LLM services?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nFacade for provider SDKs, Strategy for model routing, Circuit breaker for upstream failures, Outbox for async jobs, Adapter for vector stores. Keep prompts/tools versioned like code.\n\n### Q3. OOP vs functional style?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nOOP for service boundaries and stateful agents; FP (pure transforms, immutability) for pipelines and evals. Mix deliberately — don’t force one dogma.\n\n### Q4. Secure coding basics for AI APIs?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nAuthn/z, input size limits, prompt-injection awareness, redact secrets from logs, validate tool args, rate-limit, and never trust model output as executable without policy.\n\n## Official references\n- [RFC 9110](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110) · [GraphQL learn](https://graphql.org/learn/) · [FastAPI](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/)\n",
