    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\nLanguage choices for training loops, inference services, and greenfield AI platforms.\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAuto-generated from this lesson’s **title, tags, and headings** — refresh anytime with `npm run hub:diagrams`.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Start[GenAI] --> N0[Why is Python still the defa]\n  N0 --> N1[When do C++ and CUDA matter]\n  N1 --> N2[Go Rust TypeScript Java wher]\n  N2 --> N3[What about R Julia Kotlin Sw]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Programming Q A Languages for AI systems))\n    Python\n    C++\n    GoLang\n    Go\n    Rust\n    TypeScript\n    Practice\n      Checklist\n      Failure modes\n```\n\n\n### Q1. Why is Python still the default for AI/ML engineering?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nFastest iteration path: PyTorch/TF/HF/NumPy/Pandas, notebooks → scripts → FastAPI. Production still needs packaging, typing, tests, and often a compiled edge (C++/CUDA/Rust) for kernels and latency-critical paths.\n\n### Q2. When do C++ and CUDA matter?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nCustom ops, high-performance inference, memory control, and GPU kernels. Many serving stacks (Triton, TensorRT, ONNX Runtime) sit on C++/CUDA under a Python/HTTP façade.\n\n### Q3. Go, Rust, TypeScript, Java — where each wins?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nGo: simple concurrent microservices and CLIs. Rust: memory-safe systems and WASM/edge agents. TypeScript: MCP tools, dashboards, LangChain.js, node workers. Java/Scala: long-lived data platforms (Spark, Flink, Kafka clients) and enterprise APIs.\n\n### Q4. What about R, Julia, Kotlin, Swift, shell?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nR: stats/biostats niches. Julia: numeric/HPC experiments. Kotlin/Swift: mobile/on-device ML apps. Bash/PowerShell: glue for CI, GPU node bring-up, and ops — not model code.\n\n## Official references\n- [PyTorch](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/index.html) · [FastAPI](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/) · [Git](https://git-scm.com/doc)\n",
