    "sourceUrl": "https://learnhub.local/playwright/qa-trace-debug",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-23T13:45:03.078Z",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\n[Trace Viewer](https://playwright.dev/docs/trace-viewer).\n\n\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAligned with [Playwright Locators](https://playwright.dev/docs/locators): role-first, then test-id contracts, CSS/XPath last.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Need[Need element] --> Prefer[Prefer user-facing]\n  Prefer --> Role[getByRole + name]\n  Prefer --> Text[getByText / Label / Placeholder]\n  Prefer --> Tid[getByTestId contract]\n  Prefer -->|last resort| Css[locator CSS/XPath]\n  Role --> Act[Click / fill / assert]\n  Text --> Act\n  Tid --> Act\n  Css --> Act\n  Act --> Wait[Auto-wait + retry]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Playwright locators))\n    Recommended\n      getByRole\n      getByText\n      getByLabel\n      getByPlaceholder\n      getByAltText\n      getByTitle\n      getByTestId\n    Engine\n      Auto-wait\n      Retry\n      Strict mode\n    Avoid first\n      Brittle CSS\n      Absolute XPath\n```\n\n\n### Q1. When should you collect traces?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nOn first retry / on failure in CI — balance disk vs debuggability (`trace: 'on-first-retry'` is a common policy).\n\n### Q2. What does Trace Viewer show?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nTimeline of actions, DOM snapshots, network, consoles — enough to see what the test saw.\n\n### Q3. Local debug tools?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nUI mode, Playwright Inspector, `debug` config — step through locators live.\n\n## Official references\n- [Trace Viewer](https://playwright.dev/docs/trace-viewer)\n\n\n## Documentation deep dive\nAlways attach traces in CI failure UX for the team.\n\n**Why this matters**\nSpeeds mean-time-to-fix dramatically.\n\n**Implementation checklist**\n- Standardize trace policy in playwright.config\n- Teach reading traces in onboarding\n\n**Common mistakes**\n- Only looking at final screenshot\n\n## 3-minute study path\n1. Skim Q&As.\n2. Open the official Playwright doc link.\n3. Re-draw the flowchart from memory.\n",
