    "excerpt": "Web-first assertions Q&A — auto-retrying expect matchers from Playwright Test (~3-minute read).",
    "sourceUrl": "https://learnhub.local/playwright/qa-assertions",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-23T13:45:03.051Z",
    "level": "Intermediate",
    "content": "## Scope\n[Assertions](https://playwright.dev/docs/test-assertions).\n\n\n\n\n## Visual overview\nAligned with [Playwright Locators](https://playwright.dev/docs/locators): role-first, then test-id contracts, CSS/XPath last.\n\n### Process flowchart\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  Need[Need element] --> Prefer[Prefer user-facing]\n  Prefer --> Role[getByRole + name]\n  Prefer --> Text[getByText / Label / Placeholder]\n  Prefer --> Tid[getByTestId contract]\n  Prefer -->|last resort| Css[locator CSS/XPath]\n  Role --> Act[Click / fill / assert]\n  Text --> Act\n  Tid --> Act\n  Css --> Act\n  Act --> Wait[Auto-wait + retry]\n```\n\n### Topic mindmap\n```mermaid\nmindmap\n  root((Playwright locators))\n    Recommended\n      getByRole\n      getByText\n      getByLabel\n      getByPlaceholder\n      getByAltText\n      getByTitle\n      getByTestId\n    Engine\n      Auto-wait\n      Retry\n      Strict mode\n    Avoid first\n      Brittle CSS\n      Absolute XPath\n```\n\n\n### Q1. What are web-first assertions?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nMatchers like `toBeVisible`, `toHaveText` that auto-retry until the condition holds or timeout — aligned with locator auto-waiting.\n\n### Q2. Why not assert page.content() immediately?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nRace with rendering. Locator + expect retries match real UI readiness.\n\n### Q3. Soft assertions?\n\n**Answer (documentation-aligned)**\n\nUse sparingly; they continue after failure and can hide cascading issues if overused.\n\n## Official references\n- [Assertions](https://playwright.dev/docs/test-assertions)\n\n\n## Documentation deep dive\nCombine role locators with web-first asserts for readable tests.\n\n**Why this matters**\nDeletes most arbitrary sleeps from suites.\n\n**Implementation checklist**\n- Ban waitForTimeout in review\n- Use expect.poll only when needed\n\n**Common mistakes**\n- Manual sleep + non-retrying expect\n\n## 3-minute study path\n1. Skim Q&As.\n2. Open the official Playwright doc link.\n3. Re-draw the flowchart from memory.\n",
